{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561618-what-path-was-lampargo-on","id":1561618,"title":"What Path Was Lampargo On?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-11T22:44:16-07:00","id":1561618,"title":"What Path Was Lampargo On?","content":"Been playing through <b>Nightroad</b> again, and I'm thinking about the scene with Lampargo, who is an option to be your player's sire, if you choose to play a Gangrel.<br /> <br /> The game makes it fairly clear that she's abandoned her Humanity in order to pursue a Path of Enlightenment, but I'm having a bit of difficulty figuring out which one she's on.<br /> <br /> At first, I had assumed she was following the <i>Path of the Beast</i>, because that seemed rather obvious for a Gangrel. However, we can get a scene where we see her transform into some kind of monstrous feline creature with additional eyes. The transformation is also described as being quite visceral, with her flesh rippling like liquid and shifting between a multitude of different animals. Which makes me think that she might have been following the <i>Path of Metamorphosis</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T23:35:34-07:00","id":1561619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561618-what-path-was-lampargo-on#post1561618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The transformation is also described as being quite visceral, with her flesh rippling like liquid and shifting between a multitude of different animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats actually fitting for Protean<br /> Protean shift is a sudden, aggressive burst of supernatural evolution where bestial traits force their way out through the dead skin<br /> The official lore explicitly states that Protean &quot;peels away the facade of humanity every vampire has to uphold, revealing the Beast within his soul.&quot; It is meant to look unnatural and terrifying to human observers, functioning as an extreme Masquerade breach if witnessed<br /> Various core rulebooks describe the transformation as taking anywhere from a single combat turn to several seconds. This rapid reshaping of a dead body forces cartilage and bone to audibly snap and reform to achieve the new mass.<br /> When a vampire activates a power like <i>Shapechange</i> or <i>Metamorphosis</i>, their bones audibly crack, elongate, or snap into new configurations. Flesh melts, stretches, or hardens, and fur, feathers, or scales erupt violently through the skin.<br /> Protean is a mystical, violent, and highly visceral physical mutation to be honest, just we like to think it is neat fluid and sheemless one form into another, like how Becket jumped from Wolf to stand up as a Human<br /> It is not a puff of smoke and you are a bat now<br /> <br /> To be honest Vicissitude transformation into a Zulo form I think is <i>less visceral, </i>especially if you have the Promethean Clay merit<br /> <br /> Lampago is an <i>ancient </i>despite her 11th Generation, and her form could be a local variant, not Mythic form per see, just she becomes a mythical heraldic beast<br /> <br /> Also, a vampire\u2019s specific Protean animal form is determined by the nature of their Blood (Clan identity), their hunting habits, and physical limitations. It is not a conscious aesthetic choice<br /> The Beast adapts to its surroundings or historical origins.<br /> An Australian Gangrel is morel ikely turns into a Dingo or even a Thylacine than a Wolf, while an Egyptian Gangrel probably ends up a Jackal or wepwawet like wolf or even a cobra, while one from deep Africa runs as a Hyena<br /> Given <b>Lampargo</b> was already &quot;mutated&quot;, her Protean form may refelcted more of her Beast within, and became more mythological or monstorous than before; she porbably started as a big black feline and eded up that demonic looking kittycat with more eyes than she should have and additional features<br /> <br /> I don't think he was on <i>Metamorphosis but </i>Path of the Beast? Sure. Or since she was very old, ancient even an older Road variant, <b>Vi</b><b><b>a</b> Feritas or Via Praedator</b>\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T01:53:02-07:00","id":1561621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561618-what-path-was-lampargo-on?p=1561619#post1561619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think he was on <i>Metamorphosis but </i>Path of the Beast? Sure. Or since she was very old, ancient even an older Road variant, <b>Vi</b><b><b>a</b> Feritas or Via Praedator</b>\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Another point in the Metamorphosis idea, is that she seems to talk about her transformation as though it were some kind of evolutionary ascendance.<br /> <br /> The narrative even hints at the idea that her transformation is happening automatically, without her needing to consciously trigger it.<br /> <br /> If you strike up a deal with her and honor your agreement, she'll even warn you to flee the area, because she feels a great change taking place within her as their flesh starts to warp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T02:20:23-07:00","id":1561622,"title":"","content":"I won't discard the possibility of Path of Metamorphosis, but I think you're putting too much stock on her powers to define something unrelated.<br /> <br /> Paths are philosophies. They explicitly have no effect on your powers with very few exceptions that are still very minor. They're about following teachings and seeking Enlightenment or some similarly vague intellectual goal.<br /> <br /> Even Paths like Metamorphosis are like that. A typical Metamorphosist will have Protean, but someone who thinks that the point is to use a power to change forms is likely very low in the Path, while some successful members have no dots in it.<br /> <br /> Metamorphosis is about change as a concept, not the method it is achieved. Lifestyle, method and preference changes are good practice, and mundane or indirect body modifications cover the physical aspect just fine.<br /> <br /> Powers are an expression of the Blood. Of the supernatural forces influencing the character. Her Protean may result from external forces, a mutation of the Blood, a particular lineage, but hardly from a Path.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the themes of physical evolution and involuntary change are not the purview of Path following. They may teach to seek or accept a change, but not cause it involuntarily. This is an indicator of some other thing going on, altering her body fundamentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}